4. ABSENCE AS TOKEN

Conventional representation often spends resources explicitly encoding repeated emptiness.

But recurring negative-space structures can themselves receive handles.

Instead of storing:

\n\n\n\n

or a large repeated region of spaces, define conceptually:

<GAP:4_LINES>

or:

<SPACE:PARAGRAPH>

or:

<PAUSE:LONG>

or:

<OMITTED:RECONSTRUCTABLE>

One compact symbol can represent a much larger spacing instruction.

Thus:

\boxed{
Token
\rightarrow
GeometryOfAbsence
}

The token is not the spaces.

It is an instruction to reconstruct the spaces.

