50. THE GRAND NEGATIVE-SPACE PRINCIPLE

The deepest compression trick may not be better representation of what exists.

It may be learning when not to represent something explicitly.

Store:

Invariant
+
Boundary
+
ReconstructionRule.

Allow the interpreter to regenerate the interior.

Thus:

\boxed{
Compression
=
KnowingWhatCanSafelyBeLeftOut.
}

This is true of:

* whitespace,
* stories,
* APIs,
* kata,
* memory,
* sketches,
* Pantheon itself.

The repository does not have to contain every thought required to execute Pantheon.

It must contain enough structure that the missing thought can be regenerated.

